5–8. One of the effective ways to solve the problem is to couple dielectric materials with nanostructured materials9–11. Therefore, various hybrids have been investigated in order to reach the targets over the past years12–16. Among these hybrids, carbon-based hybrids own advantages such as low density, good chemical stability and high complex permittivity value, which may improve the microwave absorption properties and EM interference shielding effect17–19.

